<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Replay aligned audio, S1 requests, System-2 reasoning progress and feedback from local duplex run traces."><title>Trajectory viewer · AI2AI Duplex</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/trajectory/viewer.css"><script defer src="../assets/trajectory/viewer.js"></script></head>
<body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to trajectory</a>
<header class="site-nav"><div class="nav-inner"><a class="brand" href="../index.html">AI2AI Duplex</a>{{NAV}}</div></header>
<main id="main"><div class="container">
<header class="hero viewer-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Experiments · Audio-only trajectory</p><h1>One clock. Every layer.</h1><p class="lede">Follow the user input, S1 response, S2 stream, feedback and speech. Click an event to inspect it; replay the timing or audition an audio clip.</p><p class="meta"><a href="index.html">All experiments</a> · Static viewer · Files are read locally and never uploaded</p></header>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="load-title"><h2 id="load-title">Load a trajectory</h2><div class="load-panel" id="drop-zone"><label class="button primary" for="trace-file">Choose trajectory.json<input id="trace-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><button class="button" id="load-demo" type="button">Reset demo</button><a class="button" href="../assets/trajectory/demo.json" download>Download demo JSON</a><span>Or drop a JSON trace here.</span></div><p id="load-status" role="status" class="meta">Loading illustrative demo…</p><div class="callout amber" id="evidence-note"><strong>Illustrative demo</strong><p>Invented timings and synthetic tones show how to use the tool. They are not local inference results.</p></div><noscript><p>This interactive viewer requires JavaScript. The JSON schema and capture notes below remain readable.</p></noscript></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="timeline-title"><h2 id="timeline-title">Layer progress</h2><h3 id="run-title">Illustrative trajectory</h3><div class="transport"><button id="play" type="button" class="button primary">Replay timing</button><button id="reset" type="button" class="button">Rewind</button><label>Speed <select id="speed"><option value="0.5">0.5×</option><option value="1" selected>1×</option><option value="2">2×</option><option value="5">5×</option><option value="10">10×</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="warmup"> Include startup</label><label>Zoom <input type="range" id="zoom" min="1" max="5" value="1" step="1"></label><output id="time-label">0.000 s</output></div><label class="scrub-label" for="scrub">Timeline cursor <input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" max="10" value="0" step="0.001"></label><figure class="trajectory-figure"><div class="timeline-scroll" id="timeline-scroll"><svg id="timeline" role="img" aria-labelledby="svg-title svg-description"><title id="svg-title">Time-aligned layer events</title><desc id="svg-description">Client request spans, received progress events and optional browser audition clips.</desc></svg></div><figcaption>Figure 1. A shared wall-clock timeline of client requests and received events. Solid bars show requests; dots show observations. Hatched audio spans are browser audition schedules starting when a file was submitted or became available, not measured model playback. Pan horizontally on narrow screens or increase zoom.</figcaption></figure><div class="stat-grid" id="stats" aria-label="Trace statistics"></div><div class="inspector-grid"><article class="card"><h3>Selected event</h3><p id="selection-title">Click a bar or event marker.</p><pre id="event-detail">No event selected.</pre></article><article class="card"><h3>State at the cursor</h3><p id="active-layers">No active requests.</p><dl class="cursor-state"><dt>S1 text / transcription</dt><dd id="s1-text">Not received yet.</dd><dt>S2 reasoning progress</dt><dd id="reasoning-progress">No received reasoning deltas.</dd><dt>S2 final text / command</dt><dd id="s2-text">Not received yet.</dd><dt>Latest control event</dt><dd id="control-text">None.</dd></dl></article></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="audio-title"><h2 id="audio-title">Audio audition</h2><p class="section-intro">Select a clip and use its native playback controls. The timeline cursor follows its audio position when an anchor is available. This is a browser replay clock; the run does not record speakers, network playout or microphone capture.</p><div class="audio-panel"><label for="clip-select">Audio clip <select id="clip-select"></select></label><audio id="clip-player" controls preload="metadata"></audio><p id="clip-note" class="meta"></p><svg id="waveform" role="img" aria-labelledby="wave-title" viewBox="0 0 800 90"><title id="wave-title">Selected clip waveform envelope</title></svg></div><details><summary>Run metadata and archived text</summary><pre id="run-metadata"></pre></details></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="events-title"><h2 id="events-title">Event ledger</h2><div class="filter"><label for="event-search">Find events</label><input id="event-search" type="search" placeholder="Layer, command, label or text"><output id="event-count"></output></div><div class="table-wrap event-table"><table><caption>Table 1. Exact event boundaries in seconds since driver start. Request end means response received; stream progress means delta received. Missing boundaries are labeled incomplete.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">Start (s)</th><th scope="col">End (s)</th><th scope="col">Event</th></tr></thead><tbody id="event-rows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="capture-title"><h2 id="capture-title">Capture and interpretation</h2><div class="card-grid"><article class="card"><h3>Real runs</h3><p>The DuplexOmni driver now flushes <code>events.jsonl</code> during a run and exports a portable <code>trajectory.json</code> with embedded WAV clips on exit. Copy that JSON to your machine and load it above. A shared monotonic clock covers startup, S1, S2 and Talker.</p><p>S2 progress records received character counts and final answer text. Its internal reasoning text is not stored. Thinker calls currently return a complete response, so their tokens and spoken words have no measured alignment.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Two clocks to keep separate</h3><p>Wall time answers when a request started, when a delta arrived and when an audio file became available. Audio content time answers where you are within a recording. The cursor links them using an explicitly labeled audition anchor.</p><p>The current controlled test submits whole audio turns, then returns whole WAV files. A true streaming trajectory also needs chunk input timestamps, codec emission times and actual playback timestamps; those are not inferred here.</p></article></div><details><summary>Portable trace schema and export command</summary><p>The viewer accepts <code>duplex-trajectory/v1</code> JSON containing <code>evidence</code>, <code>lanes</code>, <code>events</code>, <code>media</code>, <code>metadata</code> and <code>limitations</code>. Events use <code>start</code> / <code>end</code> seconds and a <code>lane</code> ID; media use embedded <code>data:audio/wav;base64,…</code>, duration and an optional wall-time anchor. Remote media URLs are not fetched.</p><pre>python scripts/trajectory.py exp/inference/duplexomni/audio_turn_system2_JOB_ID</pre><p>Existing run folders without event logs export as <code>summary_only</code>. Their audio remains listenable, but the viewer shows no fabricated timeline.</p></details><h3>Trace limitations</h3><ul id="limitations"></ul><p class="meta">This page is a local inspection tool. The hosted demo contains no dataset speech, private paths, model checkpoints or live inference endpoint.</p></section>
<footer class="site-footer"><p>AI2AI Duplex · <a href="index.html">All experiments</a> · <a href="../index.html">Literature review</a> · <a href="../research/trajectory-schema.md">Trace schema</a></p></footer>
</div></main><script id="demo-trace" type="application/json">{{DEMO}}</script>
</body></html>
